    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐν-ητήρ</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐν-ᾱτήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐνάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a
				bedfellow, husband</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				137
			</span></i> (lyr.); of fish, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				4.383
			</span></i>:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐν-άτειρα</span></b>  (
				Dor.
			 form used by Trag.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῦ μὲν
			εὐ</span>. <i>partner of</i> his <i>bed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				157
			</span></i> (troch.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. Διὸς λεχέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					895
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				<u>Syrinx</u>
				1
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐνήτειρα νὺξ ἔργων</span>
			<i>that makes</i> works <i>cease</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1058
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιτὼν εὐνητήρ</span> a
			<i>night</i>-shirt, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				920
			</span></i>.</div>
